Review reporting criticism and the limits of reproduced evidence (@inquiry-reporting-review: 0, is #chapter, #hephaestus-core "Define-what-someone-should-be-able-to-understand-and-do.lingua#r_0070DDB221FF1E371FDC6FCBDA") { r_00938E8A05E83C0B28227241FA
State a bounded question and explain it to a beginner. Trace every central number and sentence through identified observations or declared construction, transformations, premises, method/dependencies, result and presentation. Distinguish the generating quantity from its fitted estimate and the mathematical consequence of a model from evidence about a physical system.

Reconstruct all four summary rows and the repeated-input residual partition. Give the meaning and units of residual variance, coefficient variance, fitted-mean uncertainty and future-response uncertainty. Explain why no automatic confidence percentage follows. Preserve every inclusion/exclusion decision and the input domain. Use a table or figure whose caption accurately describes the evidence.

Define exact-byte comparison, mathematical agreement, independent implementation, independent observations and robustness. Prove why row order leaves the summary invariant while changing provenance. State precisely what was restored, by whom, in which environment and with what assistance. Explain what an archive and a checksum cannot establish.

Derive single-row coefficient and residual-sum sensitivity. Reconstruct the intentionally wrong first revision and the warranted correction. Regenerate every dependent artifact, preserve history and classify failed checks. Explain why a resealed but stale result can be rejected and why an internally consistent unsupported scientific interpretation can survive computational checks.

Present a reasoned objection, response and revised claim. Use the shared-offset counterexample and identify a discriminating observation with its own assumptions. Teach the argument through a prediction, a counterexample and a transfer to another core. Outside peer review and independent physical replication remain assigned work unless actually performed and documented.

All six areas now have six developed common blocks, but no whole core is complete. This block advances reporting, reproducible evidence and criticism; advanced inference, learning and teaching, communication, knowledge stewardship and independent research practice remain broader formation. Review substantive breadth and prerequisites across the six cores before proceeding toward major branches. Lesson counts alone cannot justify that transition.

**Return:** [Scientific inquiry and practice](../Inquiry.lingua#r_75MNKZQKNB0XBG021SWWW2HASB).

**Continue in the seventh common pass:** [Define what someone should be able to understand and do](Define-what-someone-should-be-able-to-understand-and-do.lingua#r_0070DDB221FF1E371FDC6FCBDA). Develop learning, teaching, assessment and practical handover with explicit evidence boundaries before reviewing all six cores.

